## Fix 1 — CRIT-2 country plumbing (3 files)

### A. `app/api/billing/connect/onboard/route.ts` — read country from studios table

Currently hardcodes `const country = 'US'` (around line 235). Replace with:

```ts
// Read country from studios.country (added by 20260506110000 migration).
// Fail-fast if missing — CRIT: Stripe accounts are immutable on country.
const { data: studioRow, error: studioErr } = await supabase
  .from('studios')
  .select('country')
  .eq('id', studioId)
  .single();

if (studioErr || !studioRow) {
  logger.error({ studioId, err: studioErr }, 'connect.onboard: studio row not found');
  return NextResponse.json({ error: 'studio_not_found' }, { status: 404 });
}

const country = (studioRow as { country: string | null }).country;
if (!country || country.length !== 2) {
  logger.warn({ studioId }, 'connect.onboard: studio.country missing or invalid');
  return NextResponse.json({
    error: 'country_required',
    message: 'Set your studio country before enabling in-studio payments.',
  }, { status: 400 });
}
```

Use `as { country: string | null }` cast pattern with `// §S13.3 — types.ts regen pending` comment (consistent with Track A precedent).

Pass `country` (uppercase) into `createConnectAccount({ ..., country })` — already wired.

### B. `components/settings/payments/ConnectOnboardingCallToAction.tsx` — country picker before POST

The CTA must collect/confirm country before POSTing to onboard route. Add a country picker dropdown OR confirmation modal:

Add a small `<CountryConfirmModal>` step:
- On Click "Enable in-studio payments" → open modal showing studios.country (pre-fetched from server, passed as prop).
- Modal heading: *"Confirm your studio's country."* (Instrument Serif italic — editorial moment)
- Body: "Stripe permanently sets your country at account creation. We can't change it later."
- Country dropdown defaulting to current `studios.country`. Supported list: US, GB, CA, AU, DE, FR, NL, IE, ES, IT (all Stripe Connect Express-supported jurisdictions for the launch markets).
- Onyx primary CTA: "Continue to Stripe" — POSTs `{ type: 'studio', country }` to `/api/billing/connect/onboard`.
- Stone ghost CTA: "Cancel".

If selected country differs from studios.country, also PATCH `/api/studios/[id]` (or wherever studio profile is updated) to persist BEFORE calling onboard. If that endpoint doesn't exist for country, write to studios.country directly via supabase RPC `studio_update_country(p_studio_id, p_country)` — but for S15 fix scope, add the country to the onboard request body AND have the onboard route persist it before creating the Stripe account.

**Update onboard route to ALSO persist country if provided in body:**

```ts
// In onboard route, after parsing body:
const body = await req.json();
const requestedCountry = typeof body.country === 'string' ? body.country.toUpperCase() : null;

// If body.country is provided and differs from current studios.country, update first.
if (requestedCountry && requestedCountry.length === 2 && requestedCountry !== country) {
  const { error: updateErr } = await supabase
    .from('studios')
    .update({ country: requestedCountry })
    .eq('id', studioId);
  if (updateErr) {
    logger.error({ studioId, requestedCountry, err: updateErr }, 'connect.onboard: failed to persist country');
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'country_persist_failed' }, { status: 500 });
  }
  // Use the new value for the Stripe call:
  // (re-read or just use requestedCountry)
}

const finalCountry = requestedCountry ?? country;
```

Then `createConnectAccount({ ..., country: finalCountry })`.

### C. `app/(app)/settings/payments/page.tsx` — pass country to CTA

Server-side fetch `studios.country` and pass to `<ConnectOnboardingCallToAction studioCountry={country} />`. The CTA uses it as the default value in the modal.

## Fix 2 — HIGH-2 strip account_id from dashboard URL

File: `components/settings/payments/ConnectActiveOverview.tsx` line ~60.

Current: `https://dashboard.stripe.com/connect/accounts/${status.account_id}`

Replace with: `https://dashboard.stripe.com/` (Stripe's main dashboard — owners log in with their Stripe credentials and see their connected accounts there). OR: omit the dashboard link entirely and add a Stone-tinted note "Manage on Stripe — log in to dashboard.stripe.com to view your account."

Pick the cleaner UX. Recommend: keep the link but go to `https://dashboard.stripe.com/` (no account ID in URL/DOM/history). Account ID still shows masked elsewhere (`acct_•••${last4}`) on the page itself — but no longer leaks via clickable URL.

## Fix 3 — HIGH-4 ConnectReturnHandler must verify via status fetch

File: `components/settings/payments/ConnectReturnHandler.tsx`

Current behavior: reads `?onboarding=complete&type=studio` from URL params, fires success toast unconditionally.

Add verification:

```tsx
'use client';

import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import { useSearchParams, useRouter } from 'next/navigation';
import { toast } from '@/components/ui/sonner';  // or wherever toast is imported

export function ConnectReturnHandler() {
  const params = useSearchParams();
  const router = useRouter();
  const [verified, setVerified] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const onboarding = params.get('onboarding');
    const type = params.get('type');
    if (onboarding !== 'complete' || (type !== 'studio' && type !== 'artist') || verified) {
      return;
    }

    let cancelled = false;
    (async () => {
      try {
        const res = await fetch(`/api/billing/connect/status?type=${encodeURIComponent(type)}`);
        if (!res.ok) return;
        const status = await res.json();
        if (cancelled) return;

        // Only show success toast if account exists AND not in pending limbo.
        // 'pending' here means Stripe redirected back but webhook hasn't synced yet — show neutral copy.
        if (status?.onboarding_status === 'active') {
          toast.success({
            description: 'Verification submitted. Stripe will email you when your account is fully ready.',
          });
        } else if (status?.onboarding_status === 'pending') {
          toast({
            description: 'Submitted. Stripe is still verifying — refresh in a minute.',
          });
        }
        // For restricted/rejected/null states, do not show a toast (the page banner handles those).

        setVerified(true);
        router.refresh();
      } finally {
        // Always clean URL after handling
        window.history.replaceState({}, '', window.location.pathname);
      }
    })();

    return () => { cancelled = true; };
  }, [params, router, verified]);

  return null;
}
```

Toast import path may differ — match existing usage in components/settings or components/ui.

